From e00861c3f49729e30a66633a809654f63c13ff06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: morris <maoshengrong@espressif.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:19:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sdmmc): do not let cache sync mask a failed transaction

The final esp_cache_msync() call in sd_host_slot_sdmmc_do_transaction()
assigned its result to ret unconditionally, overwriting an error that
the event loop had already produced. When a transaction with a cacheable
data buffer timed out in handle_event(), that function stopped the DMA
and returned ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT without setting cmd->error, so the loop
broke with ret == ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT and cmdinfo->error still ESP_OK. The
subsequent successful cache sync then reset ret to ESP_OK, and
sdmmc_send_cmd() reported success for a transfer that never completed.

The cache synchronization is still needed on the error path to leave the
buffer coherent, so keep performing it, but only adopt its return value
when the transaction has not already failed.

The needs_sync guard only tests the start address, while esp_cache_msync
checks the whole range against the cacheable window, so a buffer ending
past that window makes the sync fail with ESP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED. When the
transaction has already failed that error would be dropped silently, so
log it instead.

Closes https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf/issues/19141
---
 components/esp_driver_sdmmc/src/sd_trans_sdmmc.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/esp_driver_sdmmc/src/sd_trans_sdmmc.c b/components/esp_driver_sdmmc/src/sd_trans_sdmmc.c
index b26e7e43c803..d467cd3653f2 100644
--- a/components/esp_driver_sdmmc/src/sd_trans_sdmmc.c
+++ b/components/esp_driver_sdmmc/src/sd_trans_sdmmc.c
@@ -578,7 +578,12 @@ esp_err_t sd_host_slot_sdmmc_do_transaction(sd_host_slot_handle_t slot, sdmmc_co
     if (cmdinfo->data) {
         bool needs_sync = esp_cache_get_line_size_by_addr(cmdinfo->data) > 0;
         if (needs_sync) {
-            ret = esp_cache_msync((void *)cmdinfo->data, cache_sync_len, ESP_CACHE_MSYNC_FLAG_DIR_M2C);
+            esp_err_t sync_ret = esp_cache_msync((void *)cmdinfo->data, cache_sync_len, ESP_CACHE_MSYNC_FLAG_DIR_M2C);
+            if (ret == ESP_OK) {
+                ret = sync_ret;
+            } else if (sync_ret != ESP_OK) {
+                ESP_LOGE(TAG, "cache sync failed: 0x%x", sync_ret);
+            }
             if (ret != ESP_OK) {
                 goto out;
             }
